{
  "_readme": [
    "Search, and the dates a daily note is named by.",
    "",
    "Every index in here is a JavaScript string index, which is a UTF-16 code",
    "unit and not a byte or a character. snippetAround slices the body at an",
    "index indexOf produced, so a body with one accent before the match cuts",
    "in the wrong place if a port counts anything else - and in Rust, slicing",
    "off a character boundary panics rather than being merely wrong.",
    "",
    "The word-boundary cases are the other trap: JavaScript's \\b follows \\w,",
    "which without the u flag is [A-Za-z0-9_]. So `caf` is a whole word in",
    "`café`, which is surprising, and is what both backends have to do.",
    "",
    "Run: pnpm run test (TypeScript) and cargo test (Rust). Both read this."
  ],
